# Cloud environment variables (claude.ai cloud sessions — see docs/CLOUD.md).
#
# The cloud_session SessionStart hook (plugins/claude-template-hooks-{py,node}/hooks/cloud_session.*)
# reads this file on every cloud session start and acts on three trailing markers, one per line:
#
#   # cloud: env               — read this key from the cloud environment and write it into
#                                 .env.local / .env.test (never committed; never your laptop env).
#                                 claude.ai drops ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from cloud sessions: store it
#                                 there as CLOUD_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (bin/cloud-env-block does this).
#   # cloud: credential <host> — a credential scoped to <host>; the hook never auto-populates it —
#                                 set it by hand in the claude.ai environment's secret store
#   # cloud: skip               — purely local; the hook never reads or writes this key
#
# Example:
# DATABASE_URL=                       # cloud: env
# GITHUB_TOKEN=                       # cloud: credential github.com
# LOCAL_DEBUG=1                       # cloud: skip
